(h) to investigate any complaint which may be made in writing against the Food Safety Officer; and 36 (i) to perform such other duties as may be entrusted by the Commissioner of Food Safety.
6.The provision under Section 36 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 empowers the Designated officer to prohibit the sale of any article of food which is in contravention of the provisions of this Act and rules and regulations.
